  },
  {
   "id": "bus_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 401,
   "width": 624,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100012,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700084,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "interface ChannelBus\n    publish(channel, msg) -> void          # no Future, no ack\n    subscribe(channels, handler) -> Subscription\n    unsubscribe(channels) -> void",
   "originalText": "interface ChannelBus\n    publish(channel, msg) -> void          # no Future, no ack\n    subscribe(channels, handler) -> Subscription\n    unsubscribe(channels) -> void",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "bus",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "busn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 710,
   "y": 386,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 135,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100013,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700091,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "publish returns NOTHING and takes no callback, so the signature ENCODES the\nfire-and-forget requirement. A caller cannot accidentally start awaiting\nconfirmation, and a future maintainer cannot add retry logic without changing the\ninterface and having that conversation first. At 13.3M pushes/sec a per-message\nack would be a larger system than the one it protects.\n\nfriendGraph.friendsOf is likewise commented connect-time-only: it is a database\nread, and on a path that runs 333,000 times a second it would be a 400-row query\nper update.",
   "originalText": "publish returns NOTHING and takes no callback, so the signature ENCODES the\nfire-and-forget requirement. A caller cannot accidentally start awaiting\nconfirmation, and a future maintainer cannot add retry logic without changing the\ninterface and having that conversation first. At 13.3M pushes/sec a per-message\nack would be a larger system than the one it protects.\n\nfriendGraph.friendsOf is likewise commented connect-time-only: it is a database\nread, and on a path that runs 333,000 times a second it would be a 400-row query\nper update.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
