   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "onDisconnect(conn):\n    for f in conn.friends:\n        if registry.localConnectionsInterestedIn(f).isEmpty():\n            bus.unsubscribe([channel(f)])   # ONLY if nobody local needs it\n    registry.remove(conn.userId)",
   "originalText": "onDisconnect(conn):\n    for f in conn.friends:\n        if registry.localConnectionsInterestedIn(f).isEmpty():\n            bus.unsubscribe([channel(f)])   # ONLY if nobody local needs it\n    registry.remove(conn.userId)",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "od",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "odn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 900,
   "y": 838,
   "width": 621,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100027,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700189,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The reference count matters. Two clients on the same server may share a friend, and\nunsubscribing on the first disconnect would silently stop updates for the second.\nWith ~100,000 clients per server, shared friends are common rather than\nexceptional - so this is a real bug, not a theoretical one, and it fails SILENTLY,\nwhich is the worst kind.",
   "originalText": "The reference count matters. Two clients on the same server may share a friend, and\nunsubscribing on the first disconnect would silently stop updates for the second.\nWith ~100,000 clients per server, shared friends are common rather than\nexceptional - so this is a real bug, not a theoretical one, and it fails SILENTLY,\nwhich is the worst kind.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
