  {
   "id": "cd2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 940,
   "y": 1602,
   "width": 584,
   "height": 150,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100049,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700343,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "ConnectionRegistry        a concurrent map: network threads add and remove\n                          connections while onFriendUpdate iterates. The\n                          returned list is a SNAPSHOT and trySend on a closed\n                          socket is a no-op, not an error.\nper-connection state      PIN each connection to one event-loop thread, so all\n                          its state is single-threaded and needs no\n                          synchronization. Same technique as the stock\n                          exchange - for a far less demanding reason.\nthe channel hash ring     read constantly, written rarely: a copy-on-write\n                          reference swap, so readers never block or tear.",
   "originalText": "ConnectionRegistry        a concurrent map: network threads add and remove\n                          connections while onFriendUpdate iterates. The\n                          returned list is a SNAPSHOT and trySend on a closed\n                          socket is a no-op, not an error.\nper-connection state      PIN each connection to one event-loop thread, so all\n                          its state is single-threaded and needs no\n                          synchronization. Same technique as the stock\n                          exchange - for a far less demanding reason.\nthe channel hash ring     read constantly, written rarely: a copy-on-write\n                          reference swap, so readers never block or tear.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1790,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100050,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700350,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The general shape, as everywhere in this guide: cross-process races belong to a shared store, intra-process races belong to a\nthread assignment. Here almost nothing is a race at all, because the data is IDEMPOTENT-BY-OVERWRITE and LOSSY-BY-DESIGN.\nSelf-correcting data barely needs concurrency control.",
   "originalText": "The general shape, as everywhere in this guide: cross-process races belong to a shared store, intra-process races belong to a\nthread assignment. Here almost nothing is a race at all, because the data is IDEMPOTENT-BY-OVERWRITE and LOSSY-BY-DESIGN.\nSelf-correcting data barely needs concurrency control.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
